---
description: ASCII hyphen; product language in UI; native translations
alwaysApply: true
---

# Writing

- Never use the em dash. ASCII hyphen `-`, comma, semicolon, or a sentence break.
- User-facing copy is product language, not intern-speak (`payload`, `DTO`, `schema`).
- Translations (if the project has locales) must be native, not word-for-word, without losing meaning.
